{
  "meta": null,
  "name": "Lost Deal Recovery with GoHighLevel and AI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "f1a2b3c4-0001-4a1b-9c1d-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2500,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Lost Deal Recovery (GoHighLevel + AI)\n\nEvery morning this pulls the deals marked lost in GHL over the last 24 hours and decides what to do with each one.\n\nInstead of letting one data point decide, it looks at three things:\n- **Timing**: how long the deal was open before it died\n- **Engagement**: is the contact still opening emails or visiting the site (based on tags)\n- **Objection**: was a lost reason logged at all\n\nThe AI gets all three and picks one action:\n- send a short winback email\n- log it for a follow up in 30 days\n- mark it as do not contact\n- send it to a manager when the signals contradict each other\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a Private Integration token in GHL (Settings > Private Integrations) with read access to opportunities\n2. In **Fetch Lost Opportunities** add a Header Auth credential. Name: `Authorization`, Value: `Bearer YOUR_TOKEN`\n3. Replace `YOUR_GHL_LOCATION_ID` and `YOUR_PIPELINE_ID`\n4. Connect OpenAI, Gmail and Google Sheets\n5. Make a sheet with these columns: Date, Deal ID, Deal Name, Contact, Email, Action, Follow Up Date, Reasoning\n6. Put your name in **Send Winback Email** and your manager's email in **Escalate to Manager**\n\n### Customize\n- Engagement tags are in Signal 2. Swap them for whatever your account uses\n- Want to check emails before they go out? Switch the Gmail node to create a draft instead\n- Timing thresholds (same day, 2 days, 30 days) are in Signal 1"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f1a2b3c4-0002-4a1b-9c1d-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Fetch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1980,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 340,
        "content": "### 1. Pull lost deals\nGets lost deals from your pipeline and keeps only the ones that changed status in the last 24h, so nobody gets emailed twice."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f1a2b3c4-0003-4a1b-9c1d-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Signals",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1060,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "### 2. Check three signals\nEach check runs on its own and doesn't know about the others. The merge puts them back together per deal."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f1a2b3c4-0004-4a1b-9c1d-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note - AI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        140
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 360,
        "height": 540,
        "content": "### 3. AI decides\nPicks one action and writes the email if it's a winback. Contradicting signals go to a human."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f1a2b3c4-0005-4a1b-9c1d-000000000005",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Actions",
